---
import BaseLayout from '../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Learn about RateMyPlace's mission to help tenants find quality housing through honest reviews.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">About RateMyPlace</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
        RateMyPlace is a tenant-focused platform that helps renters make informed decisions
        about their next home by providing honest, verified reviews from real tenants.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">Our Mission</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        Finding a good apartment is challenging. Beyond high rents and competitive markets,
        tenants often don't know what they're getting into until they've signed a lease. We believe
        every renter deserves access to honest information about buildings and landlords before making
        one of their biggest financial decisions.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">How We Rate</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        Our comprehensive rating system is based on housing quality research and covers 27 aspects
        of the rental experience, organized into three main categories:
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 my-8">
        <div class="bg-teal-50 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-teal-900 mb-3">Unit Quality (10 items)</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-teal-800 space-y-1">
            <li>Structural integrity</li>
            <li>Plumbing & water</li>
            <li>Electrical systems</li>
            <li>Temperature control</li>
            <li>Ventilation & air quality</li>
            <li>Pest control</li>
            <li>Mold & moisture</li>
            <li>Appliances</li>
            <li>Layout & functionality</li>
            <li>Listing accuracy</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-blue-50 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-3">Building Quality (9 items)</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-blue-800 space-y-1">
            <li>Common areas</li>
            <li>Building security</li>
            <li>Exterior & grounds</li>
            <li>Internal noise levels</li>
            <li>External noise levels</li>
            <li>Mail & package security</li>
            <li>Laundry facilities</li>
            <li>Parking</li>
            <li>Trash & recycling</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-green-50 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-green-900 mb-3">Landlord Experience (8 items)</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-green-800 space-y-1">
            <li>Maintenance response</li>
            <li>Communication</li>
            <li>Professionalism</li>
            <li>Lease clarity</li>
            <li>Privacy & boundaries</li>
            <li>Security deposit handling</li>
            <li>Rent practices</li>
            <li>Non-retaliation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-6 my-8">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Scoring Transparency</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
          Our scores aren't just simple averages. Health and safety factors like pest control, mold,
          structural integrity, and temperature control receive additional weight in our scoring algorithm,
          based on peer-reviewed public health research from the WHO, EPA, and leading housing quality studies.
          This means a building with serious health hazards will score lower than one with only cosmetic issues,
          even if both have the same number of complaints.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
          We also apply recency weighting so that newer reviews have more influence than older ones, ensuring
          scores reflect the current state of a property.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/methodology"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-teal-600 hover:text-teal-800 font-medium transition-colors"
        >
          Learn more about our evidence-based scoring methodology
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">Privacy Protection</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        We take reviewer privacy seriously. To protect tenants from potential retaliation:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 mb-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Move-in and move-out dates are displayed as seasons (e.g., "Fall 2023") rather than exact dates</li>
        <li>No personally identifiable information is displayed on reviews</li>
        <li>All reviews are moderated by our team before being published</li>
        <li>Users can delete their reviews at any time</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">Review Guidelines</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        To maintain the quality and trustworthiness of reviews, we require that all reviews:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 mb-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Come from verified tenants who lived at the property</li>
        <li>Focus on factual experiences rather than personal attacks</li>
        <li>Don't contain discriminatory language or threats</li>
        <li>Don't include personally identifiable information about landlords or staff</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">Fairness for Landlords</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        We believe in fairness for all parties. If a landlord or property manager believes a review
        is inaccurate or violates our guidelines, they can <a href="/dispute" class="text-teal-600 hover:underline">submit a dispute</a>
        for our team to investigate. They can also reach us at
        <a href="mailto:landlords@ratemyplace.org" class="text-teal-600 hover:underline">landlords@ratemyplace.org</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">Who's Behind This</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        RateMyPlace was created by <a href="https://meredithmcgee.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-teal-600 hover:text-teal-800">Meredith McGee</a>,
        a Boston-based public health professional, researcher, and developer who saw firsthand how difficult
        it can be for tenants to find reliable information about apartments and landlords before signing a lease.
        Drawing on her background in public health research, Meredith designed RateMyPlace's evidence-based
        scoring system to prioritize the health and safety factors that matter most to tenants. What started
        as a personal frustration turned into a mission to give renters the transparency they deserve.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        You can learn more about Meredith and her other work at{' '}
        <a href="https://meredithmcgee.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-teal-600 hover:text-teal-800">
          meredithmcgee.org
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4">Contact Us</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        Have questions, feedback, or need to report a problem? Email us at{' '}
        <a href="mailto:contact@ratemyplace.org" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">
          contact@ratemyplace.org
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
